Z||000003||rogergarrison||02-19-2001||09:50 AM||||It is a very nicely done kit. He does have a few inaccuracies. For example he says side rear windows are 1/2 louvered and 1/2 glass. There are different variations for different years, some DO cover entire area. He dont show his gauges, they dont have 'Ferrari' logo on each dial like the real ones. The quickest givaway from side view is lack of side window vent glass which has a slighly angled black trim. No replicas ever have that. There were also several 308/328 convertibles made by factory, but sold only in europe to very wealthy persons as a custom built option. On the whole he is entitled to brag a little, hes done lots of nice detail work and the car looks like its probabley worth his asking price. He doesnt mention much about drivetrain except its a 4 speed, which all Ferraris are 5. Its hard to see how hes invested $50K though, Ive got less than $30k and Ive went to lots of detail work too.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
